			title: "Graphene Modulator"
			x: 16.0d
			y: 2.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1EB339EC7EEE0427", "5FBB5CC4F79C7D79"]
			description: ["A waveguide wafer carrying detectors, graphene modulators and quantum-dot sources, diced, pigtailed and cryopackaged, is the &6Quantum Photonic Chip&r: a whole optical circuit on a few millimetres. The photonic integration hall, a circuit 2 program, a pigtailed quantum die and superfluid helium (not used up). The optical computer, which is a chip on an optical assembly. Parts by ME in matched counts; keep a few chips in stock, one per computer."]
			icon: "grindless:quantum_photonic_chip"
			id: "5F27E2F032F8C5FD"
			rewards: [{ id: "30DD83A335FE115E", type: "xp", xp: 180 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "39FB1EFE40BABA0D", item: "grindless:quantum_photonic_chip", type: "item" }]
			title: "Quantum Photonic Chip"
			x: 18.75d
			y: 6.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5F27E2F032F8C5FD"]
			description: ["The &6Optical Computer&r thinks in photons and runs cold. It is the UEV circuit, and the hall is the only machine that makes it. A quantum photonic chip, two optical assemblies and a circuit 3 program, in the Photonic Integration Hall. Every UEV circuit slot: the UEV hull, hatches and machines all take it. One chip and two assemblies per computer: keep a dedicated chest and never a big stock."]
			icon: "gtnn:optical_computer"
			id: "12A3828ECE0C81B8"
			rewards: [{ id: "7E3E33AFA66E575E", type: "xp", xp: 220 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "7702308B9A611F05", item: "gtnn:optical_computer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Optical Computer"
			x: 20.5d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5D8B9A9839432298"]
			description: ["Two photons entangled over a distance let a network stay in step. A &6Quantum Repeater Node&r keeps one end of the link. The Entanglement Station, an SPDC source, an Eu:YSO memory crystal, a quantum dot source, two SNSPDs, two hollow-core fibres and superfluid helium. The UEV wireless energy hatch and the wireless covers, which each take one node. Parts by ME and nodes back by ME; one node is worth a long run."]
			icon: "grindless:quantum_repeater_node"
			id: "7B8852855265F1E3"
			rewards: [{ id: "7C1CF223384BD91B", type: "xp", xp: 180 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "186E02F9F2068179", item: "grindless:quantum_repeater_node", type: "item" }]
			title: "Quantum Repeater Node"
			x: 36.0d
			y: 7.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3C3FC8DE94FAC5EE"]
			description: ["Light travels in silicon nitride with almost no loss, so the fab starts with a platform of it. Float-zone silicon wafers from the &6Cutter&r; the &6Electric Blast Furnace&r at 1800 K with oxygen; a reactor with silane and ammonia; the &6Synchrotron&r with an X-ray mask and PMMA (circuit 6); a reactor with water and hydrofluoric acid; the photonic foundry with ultrapure water and argon (circuit 7). The annealed SiN chip, bonded to lithium niobate as the waveguide circuit. Every stage is a plain machine fed by ME, one pattern provider each. The X-ray mask is the only part that is not used up; keep a spare."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:sin_etched_wafer"
			id: "758176235F121A8E"
			rewards: [{ id: "1C5303D2F5994A27", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "39D9E088882C7E62", item: "grindless:sin_lithographed_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3B7A8832875A0A3B", item: "grindless:sin_etched_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Silicon Nitride Platform"
			x: 22.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["758176235F121A8E", "1DCFFEC97F5A28AF", "1EB339EC7EEE0427"]
			description: ["The waveguide circuit carries the light; the nanowire that counts single photons is grown on top of it. Two passes through the &6SNSPD Foundry&r make the detector wafer. The waveguide circuit (an annealed SiN chip and an LNOI wafer in the Photonic Integration Hall, circuit 1); then tungsten silicide dust with argon in the foundry (circuit 10) for the WSi waveguide wafer, and PMMA resist (circuit 11) to pattern the nanowire. The detector waveguide wafer: every later stage of the fab builds on it, and the stages after it. Keep tungsten silicide and PMMA stocked by ME. The foundry is a big machine, so queue both passes from one pattern provider."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:detector_waveguide_wafer"
			id: "78FB2E9525C9BB52"
			rewards: [{ id: "7543CCC0522F7DBC", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1B1194F70A80CD71", item: "grindless:wsi_waveguide_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5F883E750933ABD4", item: "grindless:detector_waveguide_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Waveguides and Detectors"
			x: 25.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["78FB2E9525C9BB52", "3EEACFBDD09FDD21", "5FBB5CC4F79C7D79"]
			description: ["A ring modulator needs a sheet of graphene held between two sheets of boron nitride. The &6Van der Waals Stacker&r lays them one on the other, with no glue. A graphene film (PMMA-coated graphene washed in acetone) and annealed hBN film (ammonia borane to borazine, grown on copper foil, then annealed in the electric blast furnace at 1800 K with argon). The stacker adds the graphene (circuit 4), then the boron nitride (circuit 5). The encapsulated ring wafer, and the graphene modulator that the quantum photonic chip and the UEV emitter take. Films are small and cheap; stock both by ME. The stacker returns one wafer per pass, so give it a dedicated output."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:encapsulated_ring_wafer"
			id: "7ED63B7C5AC8E11F"
			rewards: [{ id: "32FC378AE1E6827F", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "56BC43E9D05177A4", item: "grindless:graphene_film", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1D1242DB8BC81839", item: "grindless:annealed_hbn_film", type: "item" }
				{ id: "769001ED5FB0BF8C", item: "grindless:encapsulated_ring_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Graphene on Boron Nitride"
			x: 28.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7ED63B7C5AC8E11F"]
			description: ["Voltage has to reach the modulator and the detector. The photonic foundry deposits the gold and titanium electrodes. The encapsulated ring wafer, gold foil, titanium foil and nitrogen in the photonic foundry (circuit 29). The electroded photonic wafer, ready to receive its light sources. Foils by ME; this is a single machine step with a short buffer, so it rarely needs attention."]
			icon: "grindless:electroded_photonic_wafer"
			id: "55DB7E7EB6139170"
			rewards: [{ id: "154A925C59AFDAF9", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "386B8B230C46F65D", item: "grindless:electroded_photonic_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Electrodes"
			x: 31.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["55DB7E7EB6139170", "750B64193AFA4A16"]
			description: ["A single-photon source is an indium arsenide dot a few nanometres wide. A micropillar wafer is bonded onto the electroded wafer in the stacker to make the hybrid. The InAs quantum dot wafer (MBE with arsine, gallium arsenide wafer and seven-nines indium), a chemical reactor with distilled water for the micropillar wafer, and the stacker (circuit 6) to join it to the electroded wafer. The same micropillar wafer, with gold and indium dust, makes the QD source of the UEV parts. The hybrid quantum wafer. Contain the arsine loop. One micropillar wafer is spent per hybrid wafer and one more per source, so size the MBE to both."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:hybrid_quantum_wafer"
			id: "51DE7F51CAB0E9D6"
			rewards: [{ id: "7E2B114B0CCE5937", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "503C0DD40472BD54", item: "grindless:micropillar_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1EF8109D17AFC7EA", item: "grindless:hybrid_quantum_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Quantum Dot Sources"
			x: 34.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["51DE7F51CAB0E9D6", "1AC90115EC98790D"]
			description: ["The finished wafer is sealed under a cladding layer and cut into dies. One wafer gives four. MOCVD with silane and oxygen (circuit 9) for the clad quantum wafer, which gives back water; then the &6Cutter&r with water. The quantum photonic die. Run the cutter on its own line and send the four dies on by ME; a cracked cut cannot be undone, so never feed it by hand."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:quantum_photonic_die"
			id: "161B740F2625BB3A"
			rewards: [{ id: "37DA692D00051FD2", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1D4DEA85100007D4", item: "grindless:clad_quantum_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "58F235A97E577F1C", item: "grindless:quantum_photonic_die", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Cladding and Dicing"
			x: 37.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["161B740F2625BB3A"]
			description: ["A die is useless until fibre reaches it and it sits in cold helium. The Photonic Integration Hall pigtails and packages it. A quantum photonic die and a normal optical pipe in the hall (circuit 11) for the pigtailed die; then superfluid helium (circuit 2) for the quantum photonic chip. The quantum photonic chip, the core of the UEV circuit. Superfluid helium by pipe; keep the optical pipes by ME. A few chips in stock is enough: the next stage takes one each."]
			icon: "grindless:quantum_photonic_chip"
			id: "56BC7ACF8C126952"
			rewards: [{ id: "5E8F4FA9A2FB8340", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5F8EED5E3AFFFA4C", item: "grindless:pigtailed_quantum_die", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3461515E6685206C", item: "grindless:quantum_photonic_chip", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Pigtail and Cryopackage"
			x: 40.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["56BC7ACF8C126952"]
			description: ["The last stage mounts the chip on two optical assemblies: the &6Optical Computer&r, the circuit of the whole age. A quantum photonic chip and two optical assemblies in the Photonic Integration Hall (circuit 3). Every UEV circuit slot. To automate the whole line, keep the fab in one connected block of machines with wafers moving by ME, the hall as the last stop, and one chest of computers at the end. Give each wafer stage its own pattern provider and a two-wafer buffer, route the byproducts (silicon dust, water, hydrogen) to storage or a void, and craft computers only as the hulls ask for them."]
			icon: "gtnn:optical_computer"
			id: "308108C0C3698D6D"
			rewards: [{ id: "5C1C1720239C56C8", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "316BD37F9FB5CB8D", item: "gtnn:optical_computer", type: "item" }]
			title: "The Optical Computer Line"
			x: 43.0d
			y: 40.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7939EEE351E35C70"]
			description: ["The cell, the network and the deep field detector."]
			icon: "gtceu:uev_parallel_hatch"
			id: "1F193E617E35A100"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "15CDF014D66D6A02", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "UEV Integration"
			x: 11.25d
			y: 17.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72FFCD77A1A0A7D8"]
			description: ["The first fuel run on the Mk4 ring turns D-He-3 into helium plasma and protons, and the plasma is the energy: a direct converter takes it as current. A formed Mk4 ring on UEV hatches, a premixed D-He-3 fuel and a very large buffer: a run is refused when the start energy is above what the ring stores. The ring's power for the gate, and the plasma the Stellar Forge burns for extra heat. Fuel in by bus from the helium-3 and deuterium lines; the helium ash goes back to the cryogenic plant."]
			icon: "gtceu:uev_dhe3_plasma_bucket"
			id: "72E2761F9FC0A537"
			rewards: [{ id: "3A74CF837C38CC6E", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "33B1496F2F463CE7", item: "gtceu:uev_dhe3_plasma_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "First Mk4 Burn"
			x: 21.5d
			y: 19.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72E2761F9FC0A537"]
			description: ["Proton and boron-11 fuse into three helium nuclei and almost no neutrons, so the first wall wears far less than with helium-3. Boron-11 from the isotope column, and the same Mk4 ring and converter as the first burn. A second source of Mk4 power with no tritium side reactions. Keep boron-11 on its own line from the column; the plasma goes straight to the converter."]
			icon: "gtceu:uev_pb11_plasma_bucket"
			id: "78C5C5037351F0AD"
			rewards: [{ id: "71E7F9417597575C", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5B402C5F60EA959F", item: "gtceu:uev_pb11_plasma_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Aneutronic"
			x: 24.5d
			y: 18.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["78C5C5037351F0AD"]
			description: ["The &6Direct Energy Converter&r turns Mk4 plasma straight into current, leaving helium-4 ash, and the &6Naquadria Magnet Works&r builds the UEV cell. Both are older machines with a new row. The Mk4 plasma buckets, the converter and the magnet works from ZPM. Power from the Mk4 ring, and the UEV cell below. Plasma by pipe from the ring; send the helium ash back to the Cryogenic Plant."]
			icon: "gtceu:direct_energy_converter"
			id: "13C93E95696BC875"
