		{
			dependencies: ["74EDD2F1292FA7D3"]
			description: ["Calcium-48 is the bullet of every run. It is so rare that the &6Calutron&r needs two passes to enrich it. Calcium chloride through the Calutron twice (circuits 1 and 2); a mixer with tantalum foil for the crucible load; an assembler with platinum foil and argon for the oven charge; a reactor with helium for the plasma bunch (two per charge); and an assembler with a UV emitter and an SRF cryomodule for the beam charges. The Superheavy Factory runs: every irradiation recipe takes a beam charge (the heaviest runs use a titanium-50 charge or nickel-64 instead). The Calutron is slow, so run several and recycle the depleted chloride."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:ca48_beam"
			id: "55A93A551874F57D"
			rewards: [{ id: "339D6D657FA027CC", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1CD3FB976DD2589E", item: "grindless:ca48_oven_charge", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7D4B5924F8BD5C49", item: "grindless:ca48_beam", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Calcium-48 Beam"
			x: 31.0d
			y: -24.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["72B06FB4F8A19AD6", "5BA764E947B7B979"]
			description: ["The beam needs something to hit. Plutonium-244 is plated onto a target that the Superheavy Factory holds in the beam. Plutonium-244 oxide dissolved in nitric acid into a glass ampoule (chemical reactor), then argon, two aluminium foils and a duranium plate in an assembler (circuit 22). Flerovium: calcium-48 on plutonium-244 is the first irradiation recipe of the ladder. The Calutron separates the plutonium; keep ampoules and targets by ME. The target is used in the run, so plan one per irradiation."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:plutonium_244_target"
			id: "1F3898DDD8F889D0"
			rewards: [{ id: "39534B29F483751E", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5E09B0D8EDDE5F4F", item: "grindless:pu244_plating_ampoule", type: "item" }
				{ id: "37DE16E1481E9050", item: "grindless:plutonium_244_target", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Plutonium-244 Target"
			x: 34.5d
			y: -22.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["79361740BE1544E3"]
			description: ["A heavier target than plutonium makes a heavier element, and it does not hold still: a rotating wheel spreads the heat of the beam. This one carries berkelium. Berkelium nitrate and oxygen in a chemical reactor (circuit 22) for berkelium oxide and recovered nitric acid; a target wheel blank from titanium plates and foils in an assembler (circuit 21); both in an assembler for the wheel. Tennessine. The run gives back an activated wheel, and the hot cell returns the blank, so the wheel is a loop and not a cost per run. Return activated wheels to the hot cell by ME and refill them; keep two wheels so one cools while the other runs."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:target_wheel"
			id: "123D8AA70C72EF13"
			rewards: [{ id: "727651C6F1C0B19C", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1BB5B9CEAFE6A8E1", item: "grindless:target_wheel_blank", type: "item" }
				{ id: "35C6A5CE376827FB", item: "grindless:target_wheel", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "The Berkelium Target Wheel"
			x: 34.5d
			y: -20.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["55A93A551874F57D", "1F3898DDD8F889D0"]
			description: ["The beam hits the plutonium and a few flerovium atoms recoil out in a gas. The Superheavy Factory, which also runs the recoil separation, picks them out of it through a membrane. Helium, the plutonium-244 target, a calcium-48 beam charge and a Nb3Sn SRF cavity (circuit 1) for the recoil gas; then the gas and an etched membrane (circuit 1) for the atoms. The membrane is a polycarbonate foil ion-tracked with californium-252 and etched with hydrochloric acid and sodium hydroxide. Flerovium for the superheavy census, and the same two-step pattern (irradiate, then separate) for every heavier element. Membranes and foils by ME; the output is a handful of atoms per run, so send them directly to the chemistry lab."]
			icon: "grindless:flerovium_atoms"
			id: "1AE5961A36814910"
			rewards: [{ id: "50F6C652F4456836", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7A5E89D633AEE81C", item: "grindless:ion_tracked_foil", type: "item" }
				{ id: "77D30E10920F0DA5", item: "grindless:etched_membrane", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3C33A6527B7A2868", item: "grindless:flerovium_atoms", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Flerovium Atoms"
			x: 38.0d
			y: -23.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1AE5961A36814910", "123D8AA70C72EF13", "7997AD3A03140BA9"]
			description: ["Tennessine comes from the berkelium wheel, flerovium from the plutonium target. The chemistry lab seals the tennessine atoms in a capsule and records all of them in the census. Tennessine atoms, a sealed capsule and silica aerogel (circuit 1) for the sample; flerovium, livermorium, moscovium and oganesson atoms with gold foil (circuit 2) for the census. The tennessine sample that the Warp Gate hold keeps stored, and the census that later lines spend. Sort atoms by element, one chest each; keep capsules and aerogel stocked. The census is a one-off per use, so brew it when a line asks."]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: "grindless:superheavy_census"
			id: "1891FDEB24254262"
			rewards: [{ id: "196E5EDD005DB97A", type: "xp", xp: 180 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "189CD3E3BD503353", item: "grindless:tennessine_sample", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5C61FC731819C5F3", item: "grindless:superheavy_census", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Tennessine and the Census"
			x: 41.5d
			y: -21.5d
		}
